    "episode_id": 97130,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97130.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "I try to give back to my hometown community that's afforded me, gosh, just every opportunity in life. And I care deeply about the future of our children, our grandchildren. I now have three and a fourth one on the way. And one of my first jobs in politics was working for President George H.W. Bush. where he taught me that public service is not only noble but necessary, he used to say over and over again. So it's truly a blessing to represent Missouri's second district here in Congress where each and every day I get up to work and fight for those who frankly need our help. Constituent services is very, very important to me as is building and growing our small businesses and our entrepreneurs. We've got inflation that is really hurting the pocketbooks of so many Missouri families. We've got crime that's making many of our neighborhoods unsafe. So it's critical that we do all we can to address these issues and be responsive, be available to the constituents that I have the privilege of serving. And it's something that my team and I try to embody and take on and do weekend and week out.",
