  {
    "episode_id": 97130,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97130.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. And you know, as you were talking about the various hearings, the one that of course is super soft spot in my heart is the one that was entitled sophistication or discrimination, how the accredited investor definition unfairly limits investment access for the non-wealthy and the need to reform. Now, as you know, we're talking a little bit before we hit record that one of my fellow board members and good friend Eli Velasquez was testifying at that. And I actually did like a short podcast episode just a couple of weeks ago right after that hearing to talk about Eli's testimony and just how powerful it was that for 20 years he was hovering right under that accredited investor definition and unable to participate. So I'd love you to tell us a little bit more about the bill and why it's important to expand the number of accredited investors to support the future entrepreneurs.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The hearing titled 'Sophistication or Discrimination' holds particular emotional significance for me.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The current accredited investor definition unfairly restricts investment access for non-wealthy individuals.",
        "confidence": 0.96
