  {
    "episode_id": 97130,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97130.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "Yes, I totally agree with you. And yes, we do have the Ann and Bill Payne ACA Angel University that has some virtual classes and we have submitted some information to the SEC to give them some ideas of exactly what you're saying. Could we make it that somebody could get a certificate and be able to show their level of sophistication because they went through a certain number of classes or however it's done. I really think that one of the biggest things that people need to know is that private investments, it's a risky asset class. And yes, we want to be able to say that these private companies can disclose and have the same level of scrutiny of what we would put on a public company, but that's just not reality. We just know that while we want to have as much information as we possibly can about these private companies, they're very small and they're still starting up and changing and things change all the time and they're growing and really the best way that we can help them is to get people to invest and also to have a diversified portfolio so that they are able to participate with multiple ways and multiple",
